[h1]The year is 1993. So is your user interface. All of it, in one mod.[/h1]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hermit-the-trog/ZeD.UI/main/ZeDUI/workshop/description_img/0_before_after.jpg[/img]
ZeD-GUI is a complete interface for Project Zomboid Build 42, with over 600 features and counting.

[b]This is a beta (0.3.0-beta20), and testers are wanted.[/b] Use a new game or a copy of a save. To report a bug, open the ZeD wheel and pick [b]Bug report[/b]: it copies everything needed for the pinned Bug reports discussion.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hermit-the-trog/ZeD.UI/main/ZeDUI/workshop/description_img/1_two_windows.jpg[/img]
[h3]Two windows instead of dozens[/h3]
[list]
[*]One window for your character, one for the world around you. Tabs along each, and an item's card in a drawer beside them.
[*]Crafting, building, cooking, fishing, foraging, farming, animals, appliances, furniture and trading, all rebuilt inside them.
[/list]
[h3]Your stuff[/h3]
[list]
[*]List or grid. Sort, find, stack weights, drag to select, Move To, Loot all.
[*]Read marks on books, loadouts and outfits, a belt with visual slots.
[*]Item cards two ways: a glance under the pointer, the whole card when you open it.
[/list]

[h2]How the containers open[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Mouse:[/b] on the [b]Inventory[/b] tab, click a container's button (the icons along the window's edge) and it opens as a column of its own. Click another and it opens beside it. Click a lit button again to close its column. There is nothing to hold.
[*][b]Controller:[/b] hold [b]A[/b] on a container's button to open it as another column, from any tab. Tap [b]A[/b] to see that container alone.
[*][b]Every other tab[/b] (Health, Crafting, Cooking, Foraging and the rest) takes the room, so the columns close and a container's button shows one container at a time, as the game does. Back on the Inventory tab, the columns are there again.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hermit-the-trog/ZeD.UI/main/ZeDUI/workshop/description_img/2_gadgets_v2.jpg[/img]
[h3]Gadgets you can hold[/h3]
[list]
[*]Watches, radios, TVs, a CD player and walkie-talkies, drawn as 1993 hardware.
[*]Car dashboards, a car radio, the police siren and a seat picker.
[*]Plain cards instead, if you prefer.
[/list]
[h3]Know where you stand[/h3]
[list]
[*]Health, temperature and skills at a glance. An action bar. Notes over your head.
[*]Moodles where you want them. Foraging finds marked with a magnifier.
[*]Revised Survey map colors, with route shields, place symbols, lakes, bridges and a grid. Map notes, a journal and the survival guide.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hermit-the-trog/ZeD.UI/main/ZeDUI/workshop/description_img/3_controller_v2.jpg[/img]
[h3]Built for the controller[/h3]
[list]
[*]Every screen works on a controller. D-pad wheels, quick chords, a quick wheel.
[*]Button prompts for Xbox, PlayStation, Steam Deck and Nintendo, and a button map with a live test.
[*]Keyboard and mouse get all of it too.
[/list]
[h3]Made to be read[/h3]
[list]
[*]Dark, Light and High contrast. Nine accent colors. Two text sizes. UI scale.
[*]Color-blind status colors. Four controller highlight styles.
[*]English and 27 more languages.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hermit-the-trog/ZeD.UI/main/ZeDUI/workshop/description_img/4_mod_manager_v2.jpg[/img]
[h3]Before you play[/h3]
[list]
[*]A 1993 desk for a main menu.
[*]A robust mod manager with conflict management, warnings, profiles, load order, folders and more.
[*]Saves, servers to join or host, and the sandbox options.
[/list]
[h3]On a server[/h3]
[list]
[*]Chat, admin tools, tickets, safehouse claims, mail and community boards.
[/list]

[h2]It won't break your game[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Safe mode[/b] gives back the game's own screens, all at once or one at a time.
[*]When another mod replaces a screen, ZeD-GUI steps aside and says so.
[*]Messages keeps every mod's errors in one place.
[*]Built-in support for over 30 other mods, and hooks for add-ons.
[*]Add it to a save or remove it any time.
[/list]
